1
00:00:03,737 --> 00:00:08,241
Today we'll be discussing a case
of Prof. Hiruma's patient.

2
00:00:08,708 --> 00:00:11,611
There is an unusual circumstance.

3
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:12,846
Unusual?

4
00:00:12,912 --> 00:00:16,783
We've decided to have
a professors-only conference.

5
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,585
Professors only?

6
00:00:22,222 --> 00:00:23,356
MICHIKO DAIMON

7
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:25,225
Why are you here, Daimon?

8
00:00:25,291 --> 00:00:27,060
As for this surgery,

9
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:29,763
they have requested

10
00:00:32,298 --> 00:00:36,169
Dr. Daimon to take charge.

11
00:00:39,272 --> 00:00:43,176
Kurumi Murata, 9,
has malignant myofibroblastic tumor.

12
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:45,211
Myofibroblastic tumor?

13
00:00:46,446 --> 00:00:48,848
- Where?
- Above the abdominal aorta.

14
00:00:49,282 --> 00:00:53,420
It coils around the celiac
and superior mesenteric arteries.

15
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:58,124
We also find an invasion to
pancreas, liver, and small bowel.

16
00:00:58,191 --> 00:00:59,292
No way...

17
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:00,860
This is terrible.

18
00:01:01,661 --> 00:01:04,764
- It's spread to multiple organs.
- Yes.

19
00:01:04,831 --> 00:01:08,068
And its location couldn't be worse.

20
00:01:08,835 --> 00:01:12,539
<i>Without surgery, she won't</i>
<i>live for more than six months.</i>

21
00:01:12,972 --> 00:01:14,707
The tumor size is 15cm.

22
00:01:14,774 --> 00:01:18,611
It involves the essential artery.
We must block the blood flow.

23
00:01:18,678 --> 00:01:20,480
We can't do surgery on her.

24
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:22,949
- I don't agree.
- What is your plan?

25
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:27,020
I'll take multiple organs out
of the body to remove the tumor.

26
00:01:31,224 --> 00:01:33,493
Stomach, pancreas, spleen, liver,

27
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:38,498
small and large intestines will all
be removed outside of the body.

28
00:01:38,565 --> 00:01:42,802
- How could you do that?
- Every organ is involved in the tumor.

29
00:01:42,869 --> 00:01:45,105
Normal surgery is time-consuming.

30
00:01:45,171 --> 00:01:48,875
These organs will die
while we block the bloodstream.

31
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:54,447
So, take all the organs
in the abdomen out

32
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:56,015
and place them back later.

33
00:01:56,082 --> 00:02:01,421
How many blood vessels
need to be cut and connected again?

34
00:02:02,021 --> 00:02:04,124
Maybe about 1,000.

35
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,126
- 1,000?
- The time frame?

36
00:02:06,192 --> 00:02:09,496
Six hours is the limit to
return organs to an abdomen.

37
00:02:09,562 --> 00:02:12,532
That would only give us
time for two organs.

38
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:15,201
It will be a really
dangerous operation.

39
00:02:16,002 --> 00:02:17,737
- Have you ever done that?
- No.

40
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:21,841
Hey you.

41
00:02:22,408 --> 00:02:25,345
Without experience and precedent,
it'll never succeed.

42
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:30,750
What happened, Daimon?

43
00:02:31,117 --> 00:02:34,487
Why don't you say
your phrase, "I never fail?"

44
00:02:36,055 --> 00:02:39,092
I know you're talented,
but this won't work.

45
00:02:41,227 --> 00:02:42,395
It's from Prof. Hiruma.

46
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:45,165
Hello, yes?

47
00:02:46,399 --> 00:02:47,233
What?

48
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:50,770
- Hey! What's going on?
- What?

49
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:54,741
On behalf
of Teito Medical University Hospital,

50
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,243
and as an Executive Manager,

51
00:02:57,844 --> 00:03:01,614
we won't allow you
to perform this operation.

52
00:03:01,681 --> 00:03:02,682
But you promised.

53
00:03:03,583 --> 00:03:05,952
- You're the one who broke it.
- What?

54
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,887
As for that...

55
00:03:07,954 --> 00:03:10,990
Never mind.
I'll tell them everything.

56
00:03:12,258 --> 00:03:14,060
You know what, Daimon.

57
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:19,832
I heard you let Kondo do
most of the operation

58
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:25,004
on my daughter, Yukako.

59
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:29,776
Were you trying to let Daimon

60
00:03:30,443 --> 00:03:32,712
perform the surgery
of Prof. Hiruma's daughter?

61
00:03:35,615 --> 00:03:38,384
You brought your double
to your operation?

62
00:03:38,818 --> 00:03:39,752
Shame on you!

63
00:03:40,119 --> 00:03:42,722
I had the approval
from Professor Hiruma.

64
00:03:44,157 --> 00:03:46,092
- Ebina.
- Yes?

65
00:03:47,794 --> 00:03:49,495
Read between the lines.

66
00:03:50,129 --> 00:03:54,534
There are stated principles
and real intentions.

67
00:03:55,535 --> 00:03:56,502
Anyhow,

68
00:03:57,337 --> 00:04:02,041
it's you who broke the promise.

69
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:07,247
Since our promise has been broken,

70
00:04:07,647 --> 00:04:11,551
arrange the customer
from Takamatsu City to go home.

71
00:04:11,618 --> 00:04:13,620
- I will do so right away.
- Good.

72
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:20,927
Please sir, I beg you.

73
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:26,466
Please let me do this operation.

74
00:04:29,869 --> 00:04:31,004
Please, sir.

75
00:04:31,971 --> 00:04:34,974
<i>This is a story</i>
<i>about a maverick female doctor.</i>

76
00:04:36,009 --> 00:04:38,578
Was it Doctor-X?

77
00:04:39,245 --> 00:04:40,313
How cool.

78
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:43,583
It's a dangerous operation

79
00:04:44,817 --> 00:04:49,722
with no established method
and a low success rate.

80
00:04:51,257 --> 00:04:53,860
You're undaunted by it
and you challenge it.

81
00:04:54,394 --> 00:04:55,662
You're so cool.

82
00:04:55,728 --> 00:04:56,663
You're someone

83
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:03,936
who irresponsibly enjoys seeing

84
00:05:04,537 --> 00:05:10,677
if their principle works
in a risky operation.

85
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:14,280
You think those outlaws
without any moral standards

86
00:05:14,347 --> 00:05:17,483
could accomplish something
in university hospitals,

87
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:20,353
just by working as a part-timer.

88
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:24,390
Know yourself!

89
00:05:32,865 --> 00:05:33,700
Please.

90
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,836
Listen. No matter
how many times you ask,

91
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:42,975
our contract between you
and this hospital is over.

92
00:05:45,311 --> 00:05:47,880
I'm so sick of you.

93
00:05:48,881 --> 00:05:52,552
Good-bye, Miss Michiko Daimon.

94
00:05:53,286 --> 00:05:55,621
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities.</i>

95
00:05:55,688 --> 00:06:01,928
<i>Medical care has become a world</i>
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

96
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:08,334
<i>To save this crisis</i>
<i>in the world of medical care,</i>

97
00:06:08,901 --> 00:06:12,171
<i>a freelance doctor, in another word,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

98
00:06:13,106 --> 00:06:15,541
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

99
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:20,613
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

100
00:06:21,314 --> 00:06:26,285
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

101
00:06:27,754 --> 00:06:29,622
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

102
00:06:30,156 --> 00:06:31,157
<i>She's also known as...</i>

103
00:06:35,995 --> 00:06:37,163
Damn it!

104
00:06:38,297 --> 00:06:39,799
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

105
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:52,578
OHMIYA SUKIYABASHI

106
00:06:54,547 --> 00:06:58,684
Well, it was my dream to

107
00:06:59,285 --> 00:07:01,387
accompany you to this restaurant.

108
00:07:01,454 --> 00:07:05,691
We'll never have to be bothered

109
00:07:06,225 --> 00:07:08,161
by that arrogant woman any more.

110
00:07:08,227 --> 00:07:09,128
Right, Kondo?

111
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,732
- Did you say something?
- No.

112
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:15,635
- Weren't you mumbling?
- It's okay, sir.

113
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:20,973
I have to go to Rodan
in Ginza after this,

114
00:07:21,707 --> 00:07:27,613
and entertain the voters for
the upcoming chairperson's election.

115
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,582
- At Rodan?
- That's right. Rodan.

116
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,384
The Rodan.

117
00:07:33,085 --> 00:07:34,320
It costs a lot of money.

118
00:07:34,387 --> 00:07:36,489
- I see.
- Go ahead and eat.

119
00:07:38,691 --> 00:07:40,827
- Kondo.
- Yes.

120
00:07:40,893 --> 00:07:43,663
Will you go to Rodan now?

121
00:07:44,530 --> 00:07:47,767
I want you to
warm up the voters somehow.

122
00:07:47,834 --> 00:07:48,734
Yes, sir.

123
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:51,537
- Take care of it.
- I will.

124
00:07:52,738 --> 00:07:54,207
- Take care.
- Yes.

125
00:07:55,007 --> 00:07:57,577
- Good.
- I'll be going, then.

126
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,648
- Ebina.
- Yes.

127
00:08:04,417 --> 00:08:07,620
I'm sure you've noticed this.

128
00:08:09,088 --> 00:08:11,457
In the present situation,

129
00:08:12,592 --> 00:08:15,261
the votes will be split

130
00:08:16,095 --> 00:08:18,598
between you and Kondo.

131
00:08:19,065 --> 00:08:20,199
Okay.

132
00:08:20,266 --> 00:08:21,634
Then I'm thinking...

133
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:27,707
Maybe I should endorse
one candidate.

134
00:08:28,908 --> 00:08:31,244
- One candidate?
- What do you think?

135
00:08:31,310 --> 00:08:34,280
I agree with you, sir.

136
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,882
- I knew you'd say so.
- Yes.

137
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:39,018
- This is the deal.
- Yes.

138
00:08:41,487 --> 00:08:43,523
I would like you to back off

139
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:48,194
from the next
chairperson's election.

140
00:08:50,329 --> 00:08:53,900
To trick the Takano camp, though,

141
00:08:53,966 --> 00:08:56,802
I want you to stay as a candidate

142
00:08:58,671 --> 00:09:01,574
and be present at the election.

143
00:09:02,742 --> 00:09:06,879
And one more thing.

144
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:11,751
I'd like you to cast
your precious vote for Kondo.

145
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:15,054
Will you do it?

146
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:18,658
What do you say?

147
00:09:21,661 --> 00:09:23,195
Please answer me.

148
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:27,133
- Yes.
- I can't hear you.

149
00:09:28,601 --> 00:09:29,502
Yes, sir.

150
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:33,973
Good. Thanks for understanding.

151
00:09:34,473 --> 00:09:35,608
I'm glad.

152
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:39,245
Go ahead and eat.

153
00:09:39,645 --> 00:09:42,748
I know you feel sick.
It'll be over soon.

154
00:09:43,783 --> 00:09:47,687
Let's do our best.
The medicine will start working.

155
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:51,223
She was the patient I had
two years ago.

156
00:09:51,791 --> 00:09:54,627
I diagnosed her as inoperative

157
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:57,897
and transferred her to the branch.

158
00:09:58,297 --> 00:10:00,800
- Really?
- Prof. Hiruma's decision.

159
00:10:00,866 --> 00:10:03,002
KAZUYO MABUCHI

160
00:10:03,069 --> 00:10:04,136
- Listen.
- Yes.

161
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:09,141
Can't you operate on that girl?

162
00:10:10,977 --> 00:10:13,546
- Well...
- If we succeed in the operation,

163
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:17,817
this hospital will gain
quite a high reputation.

164
00:10:18,184 --> 00:10:20,386
Exteriorizing multiple organs and

165
00:10:21,053 --> 00:10:23,022
tumor excision will never succeed.

166
00:10:23,689 --> 00:10:28,194
I will never perform
such an experimental operation.

167
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,996
You have no guts.

168
00:10:33,099 --> 00:10:34,200
You know what?

169
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:41,107
I don't need a horse that doesn't run.

170
00:10:44,010 --> 00:10:45,211
You are a coward.

171
00:10:46,212 --> 00:10:50,149
With all due respect,
this operation no longer exists.

172
00:10:50,549 --> 00:10:54,286
It's cancelled.
It was ordered from Prof. Hiruma.

173
00:10:54,353 --> 00:10:56,689
Do you believe that?

174
00:11:00,559 --> 00:11:02,628
Michiko Daimon won't back off easily.

175
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,969
Here you go, a super large size
of beef rice bowl.

176
00:11:11,203 --> 00:11:12,772
It's from that customer there.

177
00:11:16,909 --> 00:11:19,712
Regular beef bowl
with pork soup, please.

178
00:11:19,779 --> 00:11:20,613
Got it.

179
00:11:23,082 --> 00:11:27,486
You agreed to operate on Yukako
on terms as having Kurumi's surgery.

180
00:11:28,054 --> 00:11:30,089
Why did you let me do the surgery?

181
00:11:31,657 --> 00:11:32,625
And you made it.

182
00:11:33,726 --> 00:11:34,694
That's not an answer.

183
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,596
I will get what I want by myself.

184
00:11:37,663 --> 00:11:41,500
You don't want anything
to do with the election.

185
00:11:41,567 --> 00:11:43,102
You "won't do that," right?

186
00:11:43,169 --> 00:11:46,772
Thanks for waiting. Here's regular
beef bowl and pork soup.

187
00:11:47,606 --> 00:11:50,843
Anyway, thanks to you,
I can be the chairperson.

188
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:55,448
I don't care about those things,
like organization and position.

189
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:59,952
No matter what skills you have
or how confident you are,

190
00:12:00,653 --> 00:12:05,157
you need a facility and staff
to do such a major operation.

191
00:12:05,691 --> 00:12:10,896
The one who can give an order
is sitting on top of the organization.

192
00:12:11,363 --> 00:12:12,832
What do you want to say?

193
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:17,236
At the next election,
I will definitely win.

194
00:12:18,504 --> 00:12:22,775
I will then marry the daughter
of the Executive Manager.

195
00:12:23,275 --> 00:12:26,579
I will gain more power
in the organization.

196
00:12:30,516 --> 00:12:32,952
I see. You're so dirty.

197
00:12:36,188 --> 00:12:37,022
Thank you.

198
00:12:45,397 --> 00:12:46,599
In the near future...

199
00:12:48,801 --> 00:12:54,073
I will have a dominant power in
Teito Medical University Hospital.

200
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:57,810
I'll have authority
to control the organization.

201
00:12:59,011 --> 00:13:01,947
That's my success.

202
00:13:03,516 --> 00:13:05,284
What's your point?

203
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:06,786
Dr. Daimon.

204
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:11,657
I'd like you to work for me
in an organization that I form,

205
00:13:12,725 --> 00:13:17,329
as an official doctor of
Teito Medical Hospital University.

206
00:13:20,032 --> 00:13:23,469
That is my dream.

207
00:13:24,670 --> 00:13:26,338
You're so strange.

208
00:13:34,547 --> 00:13:38,417
By the way, what is your dream?

209
00:13:39,819 --> 00:13:40,719
Dream?

210
00:13:41,954 --> 00:13:44,356
If an organization is a good one,

211
00:13:44,423 --> 00:13:45,991
it'll be comfortable to you, too.

212
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:49,695
I'll make an organization

213
00:13:50,362 --> 00:13:53,032
that is worthy for you
to take advantage of.

214
00:13:53,699 --> 00:13:56,268
Worth taking advantage of?

215
00:13:58,637 --> 00:14:01,907
Why don't you quit
that doctor agency?

216
00:14:01,974 --> 00:14:02,875
What?

217
00:14:05,945 --> 00:14:07,046
Oh.

218
00:14:07,379 --> 00:14:09,982
Hello. I should get going.

219
00:14:11,050 --> 00:14:13,152
- Excuse me.
- You are excused.

220
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:19,291
Hey, hey, hey.

221
00:14:20,326 --> 00:14:22,161
You two...

222
00:14:22,962 --> 00:14:23,829
What?

223
00:14:23,896 --> 00:14:24,830
...became steady?

224
00:14:25,497 --> 00:14:27,399
Are you out of your mind?

225
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:30,836
Give me a break.

226
00:14:30,903 --> 00:14:32,638
Was it a stupid idea?

227
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:41,647
- Excuse me.
- I just took a bath.

228
00:14:43,182 --> 00:14:44,516
I'll take one again.

229
00:14:47,586 --> 00:14:49,688
- Are you in a bad mood?
- No.

230
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:54,927
They didn't allow you to do
an operation on the girl, did they?

231
00:14:56,428 --> 00:15:00,499
Good. The operation would never succeed.

232
00:15:00,833 --> 00:15:03,068
Those things happen.

233
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:05,271
- Grow up, Michiko.
- Nope.

234
00:15:05,871 --> 00:15:10,976
You should've never negotiated
with Hiruma in the first place.

235
00:15:11,043 --> 00:15:14,613
Your negotiation skill is
worse than a kindergartener.

236
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,383
You just do what I tell you.

237
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,254
- What?
- When I think about it,

238
00:15:23,455 --> 00:15:26,825
you're like an Executive Manager
in this place.

239
00:15:27,293 --> 00:15:28,527
What do you mean?

240
00:15:29,295 --> 00:15:31,330
I'm not like that wily old fox.

241
00:15:31,397 --> 00:15:34,800
- You're a sly old fox then.
- Hey!

242
00:15:36,669 --> 00:15:39,338
This agency is no different

243
00:15:39,872 --> 00:15:42,107
from an organization.

244
00:15:42,174 --> 00:15:44,243
Wait, Michiko.

245
00:15:45,377 --> 00:15:46,478
Is she at a rebellious age?

246
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:53,319
Who called me to Takamatsu?

247
00:15:53,385 --> 00:15:55,955
- What?
- Whose request?

248
00:15:56,021 --> 00:15:56,956
Well...

249
00:15:57,022 --> 00:16:00,893
It's impossible to think that
Kurumi and I met by accident.

250
00:16:01,994 --> 00:16:02,695
Listen.

251
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:05,664
I know
you and that person planned it.

252
00:16:07,099 --> 00:16:08,100
Who is it?

253
00:16:09,535 --> 00:16:11,203
Hey! Who is it?

254
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:14,039
Tell me who. Who is it?

255
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:16,342
You'd better tell me.

256
00:16:43,569 --> 00:16:48,040
So, you are Michiko Daimon.

257
00:16:48,907 --> 00:16:50,609
Are you the freelance surgeon?

258
00:16:51,744 --> 00:16:52,678
Yes.

259
00:16:55,647 --> 00:16:56,849
Nice to meet you.

260
00:16:57,649 --> 00:17:01,687
I'm Hachiya, the Director of
Totei Medical University Hospital.

261
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:03,489
Hello.

262
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:05,491
Have a seat.

263
00:17:12,331 --> 00:17:13,532
Oh, hello.

264
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,202
Director Busujima.

265
00:17:17,636 --> 00:17:21,073
No, I'm a former hospital director.

266
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:23,575
Thanks.

267
00:17:25,144 --> 00:17:26,045
Nice to see you again.

268
00:17:27,813 --> 00:17:31,250
Your "melon" boss is impossible.

269
00:17:32,284 --> 00:17:36,755
I told him not to mention my name.

270
00:17:36,822 --> 00:17:38,123
I never imagined it was you

271
00:17:39,925 --> 00:17:44,696
who requested me to
go to the branch in Takamatsu.

272
00:17:44,763 --> 00:17:48,467
I don't know
what kind of connection they had.

273
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:53,605
But Kurumi's parents begged me
in tears.

274
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:59,278
They said Teito Medical University
Hospital deserted their daughter.

275
00:18:01,914 --> 00:18:03,649
She is such a cute girl.

276
00:18:04,183 --> 00:18:09,721
I thought
you might be able to do something.

277
00:18:09,788 --> 00:18:15,561
That man over there is
more powerful than Hiruma, right?

278
00:18:19,531 --> 00:18:20,466
Listen.

279
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:26,071
Teito Medical University
Hospital where Hiruma belongs

280
00:18:27,473 --> 00:18:30,509
is like a subsidiary company of

281
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:34,346
Totei Medical University Hospital Group,

282
00:18:35,214 --> 00:18:38,550
if you compare it to
a corporate structure.

283
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:41,086
TEITO UNIVERSITY

284
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,422
I see.

285
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:45,557
So,

286
00:18:46,592 --> 00:18:49,228
can you perform surgery on her?

287
00:18:50,028 --> 00:18:55,734
But I have to take multiple organs
out of the body to remove the tumor.

288
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,474
Are you sure?

289
00:19:05,043 --> 00:19:06,545
Can you do the operation?

290
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:09,781
That's what I'm saying.

291
00:19:12,217 --> 00:19:15,120
But I assume
the success rate is 50/50.

292
00:19:15,187 --> 00:19:19,091
No. I never fail.

293
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:22,661
You haven't changed, Daimon.

294
00:19:23,095 --> 00:19:26,965
But Hiruma didn't give you
his permission.

295
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:29,368
Your boss told you not to.

296
00:19:29,434 --> 00:19:33,539
Such a relationship means
nothing to me.

297
00:19:34,506 --> 00:19:36,041
You haven't changed a bit.

298
00:19:36,108 --> 00:19:38,110
If my boss says no,

299
00:19:38,944 --> 00:19:42,881
I can ask the boss of the boss
to reverse it.

300
00:19:43,949 --> 00:19:45,651
You think it's that simple.

301
00:19:45,717 --> 00:19:49,888
If we don't operate
on her immediately, she'll die.

302
00:19:49,955 --> 00:19:51,557
Still...

303
00:19:51,623 --> 00:19:57,696
Then should I tell you in a way
you can't resist?

304
00:19:58,564 --> 00:20:03,068
Only two cases of this operation
were a success in the world.

305
00:20:03,835 --> 00:20:05,637
There is none in Japan.

306
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:08,774
If it succeeds,
it'll be the 3rd case in the world.

307
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:12,978
It'll change the history
of medical care in Japan.

308
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,517
Good morning.

309
00:20:18,584 --> 00:20:20,686
Hi. Oh, how are you?

310
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:24,389
Prof. Ebina couldn't go to
Rodan in Ginza.

311
00:20:24,456 --> 00:20:27,993
He went to the Ohmiya Sukiyabashi
in the main building at least.

312
00:20:28,327 --> 00:20:29,595
His dream came true.

313
00:20:30,495 --> 00:20:33,599
Hiruma decided to
make Kondo the chairperson.

314
00:20:33,665 --> 00:20:34,766
Is that right?

315
00:20:35,434 --> 00:20:38,604
Prof. Ebina was asked to
cast his vote for Kondo.

316
00:20:39,805 --> 00:20:42,574
I'll walk up the stairs.
Health is important.

317
00:20:42,641 --> 00:20:44,409
That's too cruel.

318
00:20:44,476 --> 00:20:45,611
Let's go.

319
00:20:53,485 --> 00:20:54,453
Damn it!

320
00:21:08,634 --> 00:21:10,102
Excuse me.

321
00:21:10,168 --> 00:21:11,336
Oh Tamao.

322
00:21:11,803 --> 00:21:14,139
Why don't we eat out for lunch?

323
00:21:14,206 --> 00:21:18,143
Japanese dish sounds good.
Sushi or soba?

324
00:21:18,210 --> 00:21:19,978
You have a call.

325
00:21:20,045 --> 00:21:22,347
I'm not picking it up anymore today.

326
00:21:22,881 --> 00:21:24,349
Are you sure?

327
00:21:24,416 --> 00:21:28,487
What? What's going on?

328
00:21:28,987 --> 00:21:30,856
It's a pain.

329
00:21:32,891 --> 00:21:34,126
Hello? Who is it?

330
00:21:34,192 --> 00:21:38,997
Hello, Hiruma. This is Hachiya.

331
00:21:41,233 --> 00:21:44,936
It's you, Director Hachiya.
It's been a while, sir.

332
00:21:45,003 --> 00:21:46,538
How is it going lately?

333
00:21:46,605 --> 00:21:48,907
What do you mean, sir?

334
00:21:49,908 --> 00:21:52,177
Everything is going great.

335
00:21:52,644 --> 00:21:57,616
I heard that you have a patient
with myofibroblastic tumor.

336
00:21:57,683 --> 00:21:58,784
What?

337
00:21:58,850 --> 00:22:01,553
She is a nine-year-old girl, I hear.

338
00:22:03,388 --> 00:22:07,225
You know it very well,
Director Hachiya.

339
00:22:22,541 --> 00:22:24,142
What is it?

340
00:22:24,209 --> 00:22:26,111
It's about Kurumi Murata,

341
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:28,447
the girl you wanted to operate on.

342
00:22:28,914 --> 00:22:30,215
You have my permission.

343
00:22:30,549 --> 00:22:32,784
You don't look it,

344
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:36,588
but you're good at
dealing with hospital politics.

345
00:22:36,655 --> 00:22:41,626
I reserved an operating room
all day for you on December 19th.

346
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:44,129
Do as much as you please.

347
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:46,965
Is that the way
you ask someone a favor?

348
00:22:47,766 --> 00:22:48,734
What?

349
00:22:49,334 --> 00:22:50,435
Yes?

350
00:22:50,802 --> 00:22:52,037
Excuse me.

351
00:22:52,104 --> 00:22:54,906
The girl isn't leaving.

352
00:22:54,973 --> 00:22:56,641
Once again.

353
00:22:59,277 --> 00:23:02,914
Can you say it properly?

354
00:23:20,932 --> 00:23:22,534
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

355
00:23:24,770 --> 00:23:29,040
I know
it's a very difficult operation,

356
00:23:30,175 --> 00:23:34,746
but please do
Kurumi Murata's operation for us.

357
00:23:38,950 --> 00:23:42,587
I will do it on these conditions.

358
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:46,525
I need a big tray
to reflux all the organs,

359
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:48,960
three back tables,
an ultrasonic scalpel,

360
00:23:49,027 --> 00:23:52,164
and three sets of tools
for microsurgery.

361
00:23:52,831 --> 00:23:54,800
Jonouchi as an anesthetist,

362
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:59,037
Ebina, Kondo, and Takano
as my assistants.

363
00:23:59,871 --> 00:24:01,239
What are you going to do?

364
00:24:01,673 --> 00:24:03,308
Will you or will you not?

365
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:06,845
I will. I got it. Okay.

366
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,447
Thanks.

367
00:24:16,855 --> 00:24:19,157
What was that about?

368
00:24:21,259 --> 00:24:25,530
The Hospital Director of
Totei Medical University Hospital

369
00:24:25,931 --> 00:24:30,635
told me to let Michiko Daimon

370
00:24:31,069 --> 00:24:35,674
perform surgery
on the girl from Takamatsu.

371
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:37,509
The Hospital Director?

372
00:24:37,576 --> 00:24:40,745
Yes. Do you think I can decline?
Can I say no?

373
00:24:42,981 --> 00:24:44,683
- You...
- What?

374
00:24:45,083 --> 00:24:49,221
You used to be a valiant surgeon.

375
00:24:49,287 --> 00:24:52,824
You said there was no cancer
you couldn't remove.

376
00:24:53,625 --> 00:24:54,659
I was young.

377
00:24:57,095 --> 00:25:01,233
But you were so cool at that time.

378
00:25:01,533 --> 00:25:03,568
Now...

379
00:25:05,036 --> 00:25:06,538
I wouldn't take you

380
00:25:07,038 --> 00:25:08,306
even as a stud.

381
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:11,042
Kazuyo.

382
00:25:11,676 --> 00:25:16,848
Do you, by any chance, think
I lost to Michiko Daimon?

383
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:21,419
- What?
- What if this operation,

384
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:26,424
the operation
that's meant to fail, did fail?

385
00:25:28,126 --> 00:25:29,661
I will then leak to the world that

386
00:25:31,796 --> 00:25:34,833
all responsibility lies with
Shuzo Hachiya,

387
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:40,672
the Hospital Director of
Totei Medical University Hospital,

388
00:25:41,606 --> 00:25:42,908
who forced us to do this.

389
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:49,748
Then I'm sure the media will
make a big deal out of this.

390
00:25:50,949 --> 00:25:53,285
Director Hachiya.

391
00:25:54,252 --> 00:25:59,391
His position will free-fall.

392
00:25:59,457 --> 00:26:04,296
The chair of the Hospital Director
will be open then.

393
00:26:06,064 --> 00:26:07,365
I will make sure

394
00:26:09,134 --> 00:26:13,505
Michiko Daimon will fail this operation.

395
00:26:18,009 --> 00:26:19,411
CONSENT FORM

396
00:26:19,477 --> 00:26:24,649
This hospital told us before
they couldn't do surgery on her.

397
00:26:25,617 --> 00:26:28,453
- They said it was impossible.
- I know.

398
00:26:30,522 --> 00:26:32,223
If we force an operation,

399
00:26:36,394 --> 00:26:37,762
it will endanger her life.

400
00:26:39,998 --> 00:26:41,199
If we don't do anything,

401
00:26:42,567 --> 00:26:44,936
she can live
a few more months, right?

402
00:26:47,872 --> 00:26:51,776
I can be with her then, right?

403
00:26:55,046 --> 00:26:58,817
She's only nine years old.

404
00:26:59,951 --> 00:27:03,288
What if this operation fails?

405
00:27:06,825 --> 00:27:08,760
To sign this paper means

406
00:27:08,827 --> 00:27:11,830
I acknowledge that

407
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,966
she may die during surgery, right?

408
00:27:16,067 --> 00:27:17,202
Are you asking me to...

409
00:27:19,004 --> 00:27:21,740
make such a cruel decision?

410
00:27:22,607 --> 00:27:24,175
What if it fails...

411
00:27:27,946 --> 00:27:29,481
It'll be okay.

412
00:27:32,717 --> 00:27:37,455
This lady says she never fails.

413
00:27:43,395 --> 00:27:44,496
Right?

414
00:27:50,068 --> 00:27:51,136
Yeah.

415
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:59,844
How did you do it?

416
00:28:00,779 --> 00:28:02,247
About what?

417
00:28:02,714 --> 00:28:05,517
You're able to operate on Kurumi
all of a sudden.

418
00:28:06,951 --> 00:28:11,723
Like you told me, I took
the advantage of an organization.

419
00:28:13,591 --> 00:28:14,459
I see.

420
00:28:15,927 --> 00:28:18,963
We'll have a conference
in the afternoon.

421
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:19,998
I'll be there.

422
00:28:20,065 --> 00:28:21,433
By the way,

423
00:28:23,001 --> 00:28:25,637
an operation is a last resort
for a patient.

424
00:28:27,539 --> 00:28:30,175
So I want to
fight with them continuously.

425
00:28:32,010 --> 00:28:33,344
What are you talking about?

426
00:28:33,812 --> 00:28:35,346
I'm talking about my dream.

427
00:28:47,659 --> 00:28:50,762
While six organs are being
preserved in solution,

428
00:28:50,829 --> 00:28:52,564
the tumor will be removed.

429
00:28:52,964 --> 00:28:56,434
Each team will rebuild
vessels for each organ.

430
00:28:56,501 --> 00:28:59,637
Kondo takes the liver,
Takano the small bowel,

431
00:28:59,704 --> 00:29:02,507
and Ebina will take the pancreas.

432
00:29:03,341 --> 00:29:05,477
I'll take care of the rest.

433
00:29:05,543 --> 00:29:08,880
Vessels invaded by tumor will be
replaced by artificial vessels.

434
00:29:09,647 --> 00:29:11,816
Then place the rebuilt organs
to the body,

435
00:29:11,883 --> 00:29:14,018
and connect vessels
to resume bloodstream.

436
00:29:14,085 --> 00:29:17,822
What if we detect
an advanced invasion on the pancreas?

437
00:29:17,889 --> 00:29:19,724
Remove the entire pancreas.

438
00:29:20,091 --> 00:29:22,560
But assess the removal area

439
00:29:22,627 --> 00:29:25,130
by intraoperative cytological.

440
00:29:25,196 --> 00:29:26,798
What about the risk for thrombosis?

441
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:31,169
The angiostomy of
the small bowel can cause it.

442
00:29:31,236 --> 00:29:34,205
I will inject anticlotting drug
in advance.

443
00:29:35,073 --> 00:29:36,007
Okay, then.

444
00:29:36,074 --> 00:29:38,009
This is a race against time.

445
00:29:38,076 --> 00:29:39,711
Do you have the schedule?

446
00:29:40,411 --> 00:29:44,349
When is an operating room available
for 24 hours continuously?

447
00:29:44,849 --> 00:29:48,987
It's scheduled already. When is it?

448
00:29:49,387 --> 00:29:50,255
Yes.

449
00:29:51,422 --> 00:29:52,590
It is scheduled on...

450
00:29:55,126 --> 00:29:56,361
The 19th of December.

451
00:29:56,761 --> 00:29:58,062
- That's right.
- What?

452
00:29:58,730 --> 00:29:59,898
Is anything wrong?

453
00:30:01,099 --> 00:30:03,034
December 19th is the day...

454
00:30:03,535 --> 00:30:04,469
That's right.

455
00:30:05,670 --> 00:30:08,907
- That day!
- It's the chairperson election day.

456
00:30:14,145 --> 00:30:18,550
We can't do it on that day.
All three of us are unavailable.

457
00:30:18,950 --> 00:30:21,052
We're the candidates.

458
00:30:21,119 --> 00:30:23,421
Don't you have any other day?

459
00:30:23,788 --> 00:30:24,856
Well.

460
00:30:27,425 --> 00:30:31,763
- Early next year...
- She won't last that long!

461
00:30:32,764 --> 00:30:35,800
December 19th would be
the best one then.

462
00:30:35,867 --> 00:30:38,903
Those three can't do
the operation on the 19th?

463
00:30:40,305 --> 00:30:41,139
We can't.

464
00:30:42,574 --> 00:30:43,708
That's too bad.

465
00:30:44,309 --> 00:30:47,011
Why is it on the day of the election?

466
00:30:47,078 --> 00:30:48,513
That's the reason.

467
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:52,116
Relax, relax.

468
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:53,251
Sit down.

469
00:30:54,586 --> 00:30:56,654
See, Daimon.

470
00:30:57,488 --> 00:30:59,157
That's why the operating room

471
00:30:59,224 --> 00:31:02,961
is open for 24 hours.

472
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:04,429
I need those three.

473
00:31:07,131 --> 00:31:11,369
But it's their personal choice.

474
00:31:12,003 --> 00:31:14,272
I can't do anything about it.

475
00:31:17,976 --> 00:31:19,210
So you're telling me

476
00:31:20,979 --> 00:31:24,883
to do this operation all by myself?

477
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:33,091
Well, that's also your own choice.

478
00:31:37,161 --> 00:31:40,565
I won't let you do
the operation all by yourself.

479
00:31:40,632 --> 00:31:42,734
I have no choice.

480
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:46,237
- Do you know how hard it is?
- Of course.

481
00:31:46,304 --> 00:31:49,274
Can't you do the surgery somewhere else?

482
00:31:49,340 --> 00:31:51,442
No matter how annoying they are,

483
00:31:51,509 --> 00:31:55,079
I'd rather hire them
because we know each other.

484
00:31:55,146 --> 00:31:56,614
We can work as a team.

485
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:04,789
Frankly, those three have
better skills than these two here.

486
00:32:06,124 --> 00:32:08,860
- What did you say?
- You hurt me.

487
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:12,196
Akira has skills,
but his license was stripped.

488
00:32:12,263 --> 00:32:13,398
I can't help it.

489
00:32:13,464 --> 00:32:16,935
No matter how skillful he is,

490
00:32:17,001 --> 00:32:19,270
it's uneasy to make a team
with a total stranger.

491
00:32:20,905 --> 00:32:21,839
Ron!

492
00:32:23,241 --> 00:32:24,709
Ta-dah!

493
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:25,677
Michiko.

494
00:32:26,177 --> 00:32:27,645
"Furiten," you missed.

495
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:31,015
You can't concentrate, right?

496
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:33,318
Okay. I lost. "Hakoten."

497
00:32:33,384 --> 00:32:35,753
Okay, it's over. You lost.

498
00:32:36,254 --> 00:32:39,424
You won't give up, will you?

499
00:32:39,490 --> 00:32:43,461
- But I don't have any options.
- It's not about the game.

500
00:32:44,095 --> 00:32:45,697
I haven't retired yet,

501
00:32:45,763 --> 00:32:47,165
as an anesthetist.

502
00:32:48,933 --> 00:32:52,370
Michiko, if you insist on
doing the surgery,

503
00:32:52,904 --> 00:32:55,707
you'll be fired before then.

504
00:32:57,909 --> 00:32:59,944
Hiromi, you, too.

505
00:33:02,947 --> 00:33:05,817
If you do such an impossible
operation and fail,

506
00:33:06,384 --> 00:33:08,653
only to be sued
by the patient's family,

507
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:11,956
this place will be
blown away in one shot.

508
00:33:19,697 --> 00:33:20,999
They are here.

509
00:33:21,566 --> 00:33:24,235
- Oh, hello there.
- Good evening.

510
00:33:24,635 --> 00:33:27,105
You two are here so early.

511
00:33:27,171 --> 00:33:31,943
We celebrate the eve of
Kondo's inauguration as chairperson.

512
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:33,978
That's right.

513
00:33:35,713 --> 00:33:38,816
Sir, I've reserved
a table at Ohmiya Sukiyabashi.

514
00:33:38,883 --> 00:33:39,917
Okay, thanks.

515
00:33:41,419 --> 00:33:42,687
The main building, right?

516
00:33:42,754 --> 00:33:45,356
Yes, ma'am.

517
00:33:45,423 --> 00:33:47,258
- Shall we go, then?
- Yes, let's.

518
00:33:47,325 --> 00:33:52,830
Are you sure
Dr. Kondo will be elected?

519
00:33:53,197 --> 00:33:56,701
Don't worry.
I've arranged everything.

520
00:33:56,768 --> 00:34:00,605
It'll be embarrassing
if Yukako's future husband loses.

521
00:34:02,006 --> 00:34:05,109
If you lose, I won't marry you.

522
00:34:05,843 --> 00:34:07,211
That's a problem.

523
00:34:09,914 --> 00:34:12,750
Hey, you two are so greedy.

524
00:34:12,817 --> 00:34:15,186
Let's go.

525
00:34:15,887 --> 00:34:17,321
Be nice to each other.

526
00:34:18,322 --> 00:34:21,559
I have to
instruct my secretary for tomorrow.

527
00:34:21,626 --> 00:34:24,328
- I'll catch up with you.
- Okay.

528
00:34:24,395 --> 00:34:25,830
Have a nice night.

529
00:34:29,600 --> 00:34:30,635
I'm sorry.

530
00:34:32,770 --> 00:34:37,008
Things will be busy
starting tomorrow. I'll need your help.

531
00:34:38,843 --> 00:34:43,714
If I become a hospital director
of Totei Medical Hospital,

532
00:34:45,149 --> 00:34:48,152
will you come with me
as my secretary?

533
00:34:49,220 --> 00:34:53,191
You're going to be a hospital
director of Totei Medical?

534
00:34:53,257 --> 00:34:56,894
Anyway, let us both climb up high.

535
00:34:56,961 --> 00:34:58,629
- To the top.
- To the top.

536
00:34:58,696 --> 00:35:01,432
- To the very top...
- Let's climb up high...

537
00:35:01,499 --> 00:35:03,634
- Hurry up, honey!
- Right away!

538
00:35:05,703 --> 00:35:08,673
- Do what I say, okay?
- Good night, sir.

539
00:35:14,912 --> 00:35:15,780
Welcome.

540
00:35:16,581 --> 00:35:19,083
- This place was still here.
- Prof. Takano.

541
00:35:19,584 --> 00:35:22,086
What a coincidence. Can I sit?

542
00:35:22,153 --> 00:35:23,087
Sure.

543
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:26,424
It just brought me memories.

544
00:35:27,191 --> 00:35:28,960
- What's that?
- Chilled sake.

545
00:35:29,026 --> 00:35:31,062
- Can I have the same one?
- Sure.

546
00:35:34,866 --> 00:35:37,902
The election is finally tomorrow.

547
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:39,904
Yes, sir.

548
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:43,441
I heard from Prof. Mabuchi.

549
00:35:45,743 --> 00:35:48,913
Prof. Hiruma cut you off.

550
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:50,148
It's not like that.

551
00:35:51,015 --> 00:35:52,350
If we're running against you,

552
00:35:53,251 --> 00:35:56,587
we should unite
to avoid split votes.

553
00:35:57,188 --> 00:36:00,691
I'm told to cast my vote for Kondo.

554
00:36:02,493 --> 00:36:04,195
How could you agree?

555
00:36:04,595 --> 00:36:06,864
That's how an organization works.

556
00:36:10,368 --> 00:36:13,638
- Can I ask you something?
- Sure.

557
00:36:15,139 --> 00:36:18,075
Do you like Hiruma?

558
00:36:20,678 --> 00:36:21,579
You don't like him?

559
00:36:23,681 --> 00:36:25,016
- Prof. Takano...
- Which is it?

560
00:36:28,119 --> 00:36:30,021
Why do you ask?

561
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:34,792
Do you like Hiruma?
Do you not like him?

562
00:36:36,093 --> 00:36:39,263
Prof. Hiruma has been
taking care of me.

563
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:40,498
Which is it?

564
00:36:41,966 --> 00:36:43,100
Here you go.

565
00:36:50,608 --> 00:36:51,609
I don't like him.

566
00:36:54,712 --> 00:36:59,116
Then, why don't we destroy him together?

567
00:37:05,356 --> 00:37:07,892
But how?

568
00:37:09,227 --> 00:37:12,997
We both cooperate with Michiko Daimon.

569
00:37:14,532 --> 00:37:16,734
For tomorrow's operation?

570
00:37:19,170 --> 00:37:20,304
What do you say?

571
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:28,312
It takes 35 minutes to
rebuild small bowel's vessels.

572
00:37:28,379 --> 00:37:32,283
Add 30 minutes to anastomose,
and restart the flow.

573
00:37:32,617 --> 00:37:35,386
Then we'll anastomose
vascular in the pancreas.

574
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:37,955
Hold on.

575
00:37:38,022 --> 00:37:40,725
Six hours have passed
since you took the organs out.

576
00:37:41,759 --> 00:37:44,762
We're short of time
after taking the organs out.

577
00:37:45,329 --> 00:37:48,332
We need at least
two competent assistants.

578
00:37:48,399 --> 00:37:51,269
- Let's restart.
- You've got it.

579
00:37:51,969 --> 00:37:55,239
- I will exteriorize organs.
- Yes.

580
00:37:55,673 --> 00:37:58,509
TEITO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

581
00:38:02,179 --> 00:38:05,616
Have extra syringes ready.
Check for Swan-Ganz catheter.

582
00:38:05,683 --> 00:38:06,817
Yes.

583
00:38:06,884 --> 00:38:09,153
We heard you're in trouble.

584
00:38:09,587 --> 00:38:12,189
- We can help you.
- That's okay.

585
00:38:12,256 --> 00:38:14,792
Extra people can cause extra trouble.

586
00:38:14,859 --> 00:38:16,294
Hey!

587
00:38:17,194 --> 00:38:19,196
- Is there anything we can do?
- No.

588
00:38:19,263 --> 00:38:21,832
- Tell us anything.
- We'll do anything.

589
00:38:21,899 --> 00:38:25,970
It's time to show Dr. Daimon
that we've been improving.

590
00:38:26,337 --> 00:38:28,472
- Have you?
- Stop it.

591
00:38:28,539 --> 00:38:31,842
Extra people can cause extra trouble.

592
00:38:32,843 --> 00:38:35,146
We'll definitely be of good use.

593
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:36,847
Please.

594
00:38:36,914 --> 00:38:40,051
We, as assistants, will never fail.

595
00:38:42,887 --> 00:38:44,121
The day has finally come.

596
00:38:44,188 --> 00:38:45,089
Yeah.

597
00:38:45,890 --> 00:38:48,626
It takes more than 15 hours, right?

598
00:38:50,528 --> 00:38:51,796
It's so long.

599
00:38:52,797 --> 00:38:54,265
You'll be sleeping.

600
00:38:54,732 --> 00:38:56,667
When you wake up, all will be done.

601
00:38:57,101 --> 00:38:59,570
When I wake up?

602
00:39:08,312 --> 00:39:11,682
Don't worry. I never fail.

603
00:39:19,223 --> 00:39:20,257
It's time to go.

604
00:39:29,133 --> 00:39:30,634
Turn here.

605
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:45,750
- Is it starting soon?
- Yours too?

606
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:46,951
It'll start.

607
00:40:12,843 --> 00:40:14,378
RESIGNATION

608
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:17,448
FIRE US!!

609
00:40:17,515 --> 00:40:19,116
MICHIKO DAIMON
HIROMI JONOUCHI

610
00:40:19,183 --> 00:40:21,118
You forgot to sign.

611
00:40:30,327 --> 00:40:33,731
We start exteriorize multiple organs
and remove a tumor.

612
00:40:34,131 --> 00:40:35,132
Let's do it.

613
00:40:35,733 --> 00:40:37,034
Yes, let's do it.

614
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:38,502
Our target time is 15 hours.

615
00:40:38,569 --> 00:40:40,371
- We don't have much time.
- Yes.

616
00:40:41,605 --> 00:40:42,606
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

617
00:41:12,203 --> 00:41:14,004
VOTING BOX

618
00:41:15,039 --> 00:41:17,441
Daimon went into the operating room.

619
00:41:17,508 --> 00:41:21,145
I see. Daimon is in trouble.

620
00:41:22,513 --> 00:41:23,514
Yes, sir.

621
00:41:26,550 --> 00:41:30,621
It's time for us to confirm

622
00:41:30,988 --> 00:41:34,625
final acknowledgements

623
00:41:34,692 --> 00:41:37,127
from the three candidates

624
00:41:37,194 --> 00:41:40,831
for the election of the chairperson.

625
00:41:40,898 --> 00:41:43,667
Professor Kondo, please start first.

626
00:41:48,539 --> 00:41:50,207
SECOND SURGERY DEPARTMENT
CHAIRMAN ELECTION

627
00:41:53,244 --> 00:41:54,478
I'm Shinobu Kondo.

628
00:41:55,446 --> 00:41:59,950
My strength is, first of all,
that I'm young.

629
00:42:03,921 --> 00:42:05,589
Stomach and bowel are detached.

630
00:42:05,656 --> 00:42:06,590
Okay.

631
00:42:09,293 --> 00:42:10,761
Confirming tumor's location.

632
00:42:10,828 --> 00:42:13,430
- Hey, your head is in my way.
- I'm sorry.

633
00:42:15,900 --> 00:42:18,235
To nurture future generation,

634
00:42:18,636 --> 00:42:22,573
I plan to have a joint program
with Massachusetts Medical School

635
00:42:23,173 --> 00:42:27,177
- and Columbia Medical...
- It's time they reach the pancreas.

636
00:42:27,978 --> 00:42:28,913
I think so.

637
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:31,282
They should be careful with the timing.

638
00:42:31,749 --> 00:42:35,119
Daimon will have no problem.

639
00:42:35,185 --> 00:42:37,855
But pancreas comes next,
which is a problem.

640
00:42:39,423 --> 00:42:40,391
That's true.

641
00:42:43,060 --> 00:42:46,664
As I expected,
tumor coils around portal vein.

642
00:42:47,398 --> 00:42:50,100
- Don't have to look.
- Sorry.

643
00:42:50,968 --> 00:42:53,470
Take the organs out with the tumor?

644
00:42:53,537 --> 00:42:57,174
We must disconnect the main artery
and inferior vena cava first.

645
00:43:00,044 --> 00:43:03,247
There's no time.
We have to decide quickly.

646
00:43:05,683 --> 00:43:07,151
- Hold there.
- Yes.

647
00:43:07,217 --> 00:43:10,821
This is my statement.
Thanks for listening.

648
00:43:10,888 --> 00:43:12,022
That was impressive.

649
00:43:15,059 --> 00:43:16,193
Thank you very much.

650
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:26,370
Prof. Ebina, make your statement.

651
00:43:26,437 --> 00:43:28,772
Yes. Excuse me.

652
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:34,511
They should be checking
the tumor's location now.

653
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:40,384
I've been wondering about this part.

654
00:43:40,985 --> 00:43:43,487
The tumor coils around
the superior mesenteric artery

655
00:43:43,554 --> 00:43:45,689
as well as both sides of renal vein.

656
00:43:45,756 --> 00:43:47,224
I'm Takashi Ebina.

657
00:43:49,393 --> 00:43:51,729
I am grateful to Professor Hiruma,

658
00:43:52,696 --> 00:43:57,901
the current Executive Manager
in the Department of Surgery.

659
00:43:58,202 --> 00:43:59,737
You don't have to say that.

660
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,107
I'm not sure if I'm worthy...

661
00:44:03,774 --> 00:44:08,045
He was told to vote for you.

662
00:44:09,013 --> 00:44:10,581
I thank Professor Hiruma.

663
00:44:11,815 --> 00:44:16,153
If I'm elected the chairperson,
I plan to strive to improve

664
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:23,894
the quality of surgical care
for elderly people.

665
00:44:25,162 --> 00:44:27,164
Elderly people who live alone

666
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:30,501
feel insecure and struggle to...

667
00:44:32,436 --> 00:44:35,639
Ebina. What's wrong? Ebina?

668
00:44:39,777 --> 00:44:41,712
Oh, Kondo? What happened?

669
00:44:45,482 --> 00:44:47,451
I apologize for a sudden notice,

670
00:44:47,985 --> 00:44:50,888
but I would like to
drop out from this election.

671
00:44:50,954 --> 00:44:52,456
- What?
- Drop out?

672
00:44:52,523 --> 00:44:53,957
I abstain my voting right, too.

673
00:44:56,226 --> 00:44:58,162
Wait. Hey, wait!

674
00:44:59,363 --> 00:45:02,232
What's this all about?
What's going on?

675
00:45:08,305 --> 00:45:11,275
Hey, what's happening?

676
00:45:24,488 --> 00:45:25,956
- Sweat.
- Yes.

677
00:45:28,692 --> 00:45:30,594
Detach it from retroperitoneum.

678
00:45:37,334 --> 00:45:39,336
Main artery and vena cava
are exposed.

679
00:45:39,870 --> 00:45:42,573
- What's next?
- Calm down.

680
00:45:44,174 --> 00:45:45,509
- Vascular tape.
- Yes.

681
00:45:46,210 --> 00:45:47,077
ANESTHESIA TIME

682
00:45:53,550 --> 00:45:54,651
Tweezers.

683
00:46:04,361 --> 00:46:05,362
Professor Kondo!

684
00:46:06,029 --> 00:46:07,631
He's here!

685
00:46:11,368 --> 00:46:16,173
Clamp main artery with forceps and
block bloodstream to the organs.

686
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:17,908
- Let's switch.
- Yes, sir.

687
00:46:18,342 --> 00:46:20,110
Satinsky.

688
00:46:20,177 --> 00:46:21,712
I need that, too.

689
00:46:25,149 --> 00:46:26,483
- Give me one more.
- Yes.

690
00:46:27,684 --> 00:46:29,453
- Detaching main artery. Metzen.
- Yes.

691
00:46:32,623 --> 00:46:34,992
I'm impressed.

692
00:46:35,559 --> 00:46:38,428
You're two steps
ahead than I expected.

693
00:46:38,495 --> 00:46:40,597
I'm one step behind my schedule.

694
00:46:41,498 --> 00:46:43,033
How can you be here?

695
00:46:43,901 --> 00:46:48,138
Well, this pulled me
two steps back in my life.

696
00:46:59,783 --> 00:47:01,985
Main artery and inferior
vena cava are detached.

697
00:47:02,052 --> 00:47:06,390
Taking out stomach, pancreas,
spleen, liver, bowels, and tumor.

698
00:47:06,456 --> 00:47:07,491
I've got it.

699
00:47:07,891 --> 00:47:09,059
Bring the vat.

700
00:47:27,277 --> 00:47:28,712
SHINOBU KONDO

701
00:47:31,515 --> 00:47:35,686
I have never been humiliated
like this in my life.

702
00:47:35,752 --> 00:47:36,720
Yes, of course.

703
00:47:38,155 --> 00:47:39,556
Mr. Takano.

704
00:47:39,623 --> 00:47:41,558
The situation has changed.

705
00:47:43,126 --> 00:47:46,897
You will be elected
as the chairperson now.

706
00:47:47,865 --> 00:47:50,667
I'll vote for you as well.

707
00:47:51,835 --> 00:47:52,703
Ebina...

708
00:47:54,271 --> 00:47:57,274
Please calm down, everyone.

709
00:47:57,975 --> 00:48:00,244
I shall proceed then.
Professor Takano.

710
00:48:01,211 --> 00:48:05,315
Will you give us
your confirmation speech?

711
00:48:20,964 --> 00:48:21,999
Right now,

712
00:48:24,234 --> 00:48:27,304
the patient who is in the operation room

713
00:48:28,906 --> 00:48:30,240
is someone I abandoned

714
00:48:32,709 --> 00:48:34,411
in the past.

715
00:48:37,114 --> 00:48:39,149
The patient is a nine-year-old girl.

716
00:48:39,216 --> 00:48:45,322
In this surgery, we exteriorize
multiple organs and remove the tumor.

717
00:48:45,389 --> 00:48:48,926
We take six organs out of the body

718
00:48:49,426 --> 00:48:51,495
and reflux in preservation solution.

719
00:48:51,561 --> 00:48:56,867
After removal of tumor, these organs
will be replaced into the body.

720
00:48:56,934 --> 00:49:00,337
This is an unthinkable method.

721
00:49:00,804 --> 00:49:02,372
Right now I'm in a position

722
00:49:02,439 --> 00:49:07,144
where I must chose the chance
to become a chairperson

723
00:49:07,744 --> 00:49:11,448
or the chance to
exercise my medical skill

724
00:49:11,515 --> 00:49:13,884
in this once-in-a-life time operation.

725
00:49:14,318 --> 00:49:17,154
I was contemplating
which option I should choose,

726
00:49:18,155 --> 00:49:19,222
which choice...

727
00:49:20,057 --> 00:49:24,895
will make me happy as a surgeon.

728
00:49:25,329 --> 00:49:28,098
Now I have concluded
that it's time for me to leave.

729
00:49:30,100 --> 00:49:35,605
The election can't continue.

730
00:49:40,844 --> 00:49:43,347
What's wrong with them?

731
00:49:45,582 --> 00:49:48,585
Are they stupid?

732
00:49:49,987 --> 00:49:51,254
- They're so stupid.
- True.

733
00:49:53,857 --> 00:49:55,559
They are unbelievable.

734
00:49:58,528 --> 00:49:59,563
It's a waste of time.

735
00:50:03,867 --> 00:50:06,970
Renal and artificial vessels
are rejoined. Restart bloodstream.

736
00:50:07,404 --> 00:50:09,439
- Wait.
- I can't. Metzen.

737
00:50:09,506 --> 00:50:12,142
You have 60 minutes
to rebuild the liver's.

738
00:50:12,209 --> 00:50:13,777
I'll do it in 45 min.

739
00:50:14,177 --> 00:50:16,046
I'll take care of liver and bowels.

740
00:50:16,113 --> 00:50:18,715
You can't do them all, Dr. Daimon.

741
00:50:18,782 --> 00:50:21,618
Then I'll do pancreas and spleen.

742
00:50:22,185 --> 00:50:23,653
Saturation is 90.

743
00:50:23,720 --> 00:50:25,689
- I know. Ultrasonic scalpel.
- Yes.

744
00:50:28,191 --> 00:50:30,694
It's too late to close the abdomen.

745
00:50:30,761 --> 00:50:32,129
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

746
00:50:52,649 --> 00:50:54,117
- Graft.
- Here.

747
00:50:54,184 --> 00:50:55,786
LISA HASHIMOTO, NURSE

748
00:50:55,852 --> 00:50:57,320
- Hurry.
- Sorry.

749
00:51:00,957 --> 00:51:02,426
Damn it.

750
00:51:03,627 --> 00:51:04,594
I wipe your sweat.

751
00:51:06,596 --> 00:51:09,332
- Don't be frustrated. Calm down.
- Prof. Takano!

752
00:51:09,399 --> 00:51:14,037
All organs are out, right?
I'll rebuild bowels' vessels.

753
00:51:14,104 --> 00:51:15,705
- Thank you.
- Let's do it.

754
00:51:15,772 --> 00:51:16,673
Scalpel.

755
00:51:17,441 --> 00:51:19,042
- Y-shaped tweezers.
- Yes.

756
00:51:19,743 --> 00:51:21,111
- Lower the loupe.
- Yes.

757
00:51:22,245 --> 00:51:25,415
- We have five hours to go.
- I've got it.

758
00:51:25,482 --> 00:51:27,117
- I've got it.
- I've got it.

759
00:51:33,523 --> 00:51:34,724
What am I doing?

760
00:51:36,960 --> 00:51:37,894
What am I doing?

761
00:51:38,395 --> 00:51:41,531
I'd like to announce
the result of our discussion.

762
00:51:41,965 --> 00:51:44,468
We have decided to...

763
00:51:46,636 --> 00:51:48,905
freeze the election for now.

764
00:51:48,972 --> 00:51:50,173
Freeze?

765
00:51:51,875 --> 00:51:52,876
Freeze?

766
00:51:53,410 --> 00:51:56,079
Ebina.

767
00:51:59,749 --> 00:52:04,688
All I can say is that your precious vote

768
00:52:05,388 --> 00:52:09,893
is returned to you for now.

769
00:52:10,827 --> 00:52:11,695
I see.

770
00:52:13,897 --> 00:52:18,201
Unlike stupid Takano and Kondo,

771
00:52:19,035 --> 00:52:23,173
I can at least give you credit
for staying here until the end.

772
00:52:23,573 --> 00:52:26,910
Maybe.

773
00:52:29,179 --> 00:52:30,747
Maybe.

774
00:52:34,384 --> 00:52:37,287
You're lucky. You're a lucky man.

775
00:52:37,988 --> 00:52:39,189
- Lucky?
- Lucky.

776
00:52:40,123 --> 00:52:42,092
You're free to leave.

777
00:52:42,726 --> 00:52:45,428
Thanks for your precious time today.

778
00:52:45,495 --> 00:52:47,197
Thank you very much.

779
00:52:48,298 --> 00:52:49,966
- No way.
- What's wrong?

780
00:52:50,534 --> 00:52:52,936
Invasion of pancreatic cancer
to the caudal direction.

781
00:52:53,937 --> 00:52:57,674
- So we can't save the pancreas?
- We have to give up on pancreas.

782
00:52:58,842 --> 00:53:00,710
- That's not an option.
- But...

783
00:53:00,777 --> 00:53:03,547
She will be a female fisherman.

784
00:53:03,613 --> 00:53:04,614
Fisherman?

785
00:53:04,681 --> 00:53:09,619
Without pancreas,
she'll have to carry an insulin pump.

786
00:53:09,686 --> 00:53:10,787
We don't have time.

787
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:14,624
We'll cut another 1 cm
and pass it to the lab again.

788
00:53:14,691 --> 00:53:17,827
- Wish we had one more doctor.
- We want one like Ebina.

789
00:53:17,894 --> 00:53:19,863
- I can do this. Scalpel.
- Yes.

790
00:53:26,436 --> 00:53:29,306
What should I do? What should I do?

791
00:53:30,507 --> 00:53:33,910
Should I join Daimon as a professor?

792
00:53:33,977 --> 00:53:37,714
Or should I trust Professor Hiruma

793
00:53:38,548 --> 00:53:41,651
and take a chance
to be the chairperson?

794
00:53:43,720 --> 00:53:44,788
What should I do?

795
00:53:45,121 --> 00:53:48,758
I can give you credit

796
00:53:49,326 --> 00:53:52,996
for staying until the end. Maybe.

797
00:53:54,965 --> 00:53:57,133
- Maybe?
- Maybe.

798
00:53:58,001 --> 00:53:59,069
What did he mean?

799
00:54:00,303 --> 00:54:01,304
What did he mean?

800
00:54:03,773 --> 00:54:05,075
What did he mean?

801
00:54:12,315 --> 00:54:15,585
Why? I can't reach the portal vein.

802
00:54:17,621 --> 00:54:20,890
No good.
This will create a problem.

803
00:54:24,861 --> 00:54:25,829
What are you going to do?

804
00:54:33,803 --> 00:54:36,573
Don't replace the portal vein
with an artificial vessel.

805
00:54:39,042 --> 00:54:41,578
Attach liver to the left renal vein.

806
00:54:41,878 --> 00:54:46,182
It's revascularization by left
renal vein portal vein anastomosis.

807
00:54:46,683 --> 00:54:49,486
- I see.
- That's a great idea.

808
00:54:49,886 --> 00:54:51,855
- There's no time. Hurry!
- I know.

809
00:54:51,921 --> 00:54:53,556
- Forceps.
- Yes.

810
00:54:53,623 --> 00:54:54,591
Who is that?

811
00:54:55,525 --> 00:54:57,494
He's a doctor without a license.

812
00:54:57,560 --> 00:54:58,795
No license?

813
00:54:58,862 --> 00:55:00,797
Focus on your hands.

814
00:55:00,864 --> 00:55:02,065
- Metzen.
- Yes.

815
00:55:03,233 --> 00:55:04,567
He's also my mentor.

816
00:55:18,515 --> 00:55:19,449
Professor Ebina.

817
00:55:22,519 --> 00:55:23,820
Pancreas isn't ready, right?

818
00:55:24,854 --> 00:55:26,356
- Well...
- They're no good.

819
00:55:28,425 --> 00:55:30,193
If I don't do it, who will?

820
00:55:30,260 --> 00:55:33,330
It's already taken care of.

821
00:55:36,766 --> 00:55:39,035
They don't need any more help.

822
00:55:40,203 --> 00:55:41,938
- They don't need any?
- No.

823
00:55:54,718 --> 00:55:55,785
Blood flow restarts.

824
00:56:08,064 --> 00:56:10,300
Organs are back to normal.

825
00:56:12,469 --> 00:56:13,303
It's a success.

826
00:56:13,837 --> 00:56:15,605
We did it.

827
00:56:19,776 --> 00:56:20,744
This is a success.

828
00:56:26,783 --> 00:56:27,817
Closing the abdomen.

829
00:56:37,894 --> 00:56:40,964
Blood pressure is 80/55.
Heart pulse is 95.

830
00:56:43,066 --> 00:56:44,267
Surgery complete.

831
00:56:50,540 --> 00:56:51,775
You did a great job.

832
00:56:56,713 --> 00:56:57,847
Good job, doctor.

833
00:57:00,150 --> 00:57:01,418
- Thanks.
- Great job.

834
00:57:01,484 --> 00:57:04,220
You did great.

835
00:57:06,022 --> 00:57:06,890
Great job.

836
00:57:08,425 --> 00:57:09,292
Good job.

837
00:57:16,666 --> 00:57:17,600
Thank you.

838
00:58:05,715 --> 00:58:08,952
I can't believe you called me first.

839
00:58:09,586 --> 00:58:12,155
This is the first time.

840
00:58:12,956 --> 00:58:13,823
So...

841
00:58:15,492 --> 00:58:17,527
- This is the usual bill.
- Okay.

842
00:58:17,594 --> 00:58:19,362
And the melon.

843
00:58:19,429 --> 00:58:20,463
- Okay.
- Here you are.

844
00:58:21,331 --> 00:58:25,268
Okay. I'll put this aside for now.

845
00:58:26,469 --> 00:58:28,171
Let's get to the main subject.

846
00:58:29,172 --> 00:58:31,107
The main subject?

847
00:58:32,008 --> 00:58:34,644
We'd like to officially
hire Miss Michiko Daimon

848
00:58:35,311 --> 00:58:39,516
as our resident
of the Department of Surgery

849
00:58:40,483 --> 00:58:43,119
in Teito Medical Hospital.

850
00:58:43,186 --> 00:58:46,089
Oh, wow. All right.

851
00:58:46,589 --> 00:58:49,993
We do receive
such offers from everywhere.

852
00:58:50,059 --> 00:58:52,262
I'm sure you do. I'm sure.

853
00:58:52,328 --> 00:58:55,198
But our university hospital

854
00:58:56,499 --> 00:59:01,070
will offer 50 million yen
as contract-signing bonus

855
00:59:02,906 --> 00:59:06,042
and another 50 million yen
as an advance annual pay.

856
00:59:06,509 --> 00:59:07,610
What do you think?

857
00:59:08,678 --> 00:59:11,481
Would you say that again?

858
00:59:11,548 --> 00:59:15,218
Okay. Contract bonus is 50 million yen!

859
00:59:15,285 --> 00:59:18,354
An advance annual pay is 50 million yen!

860
00:59:23,993 --> 00:59:25,128
Kaboom! Kaboom, kaboom!

861
00:59:26,996 --> 00:59:29,098
I see. You sold me.

862
00:59:30,934 --> 00:59:32,001
You don't want to go?

863
00:59:33,069 --> 00:59:34,137
Of course.

864
00:59:36,005 --> 00:59:37,240
You don't want to be sold.

865
00:59:38,308 --> 00:59:39,809
The contract money and

866
00:59:40,443 --> 00:59:42,478
annual pay is 50 million yen each.

867
00:59:43,580 --> 00:59:46,583
A lump-sum of 100 million
will be deposited.

868
00:59:47,483 --> 00:59:48,651
Still you're not happy.

869
00:59:49,719 --> 00:59:51,588
It's okay.

870
00:59:52,689 --> 00:59:55,758
Oh? I thought you'd give me a hard time.

871
00:59:56,593 --> 00:59:58,595
That'll redeem my debt, right?

872
00:59:59,495 --> 01:00:00,463
I guess so.

873
01:00:03,833 --> 01:00:07,337
The day has finally come
when you quit freelancing.

874
01:00:10,773 --> 01:00:15,144
A press conference is held
for the surgery on the 23rd.

875
01:00:15,678 --> 01:00:18,014
- Make sure you attend.
- Okay.

876
01:00:19,649 --> 01:00:20,550
Michiko.

877
01:00:22,085 --> 01:00:23,186
This is life.

878
01:00:26,889 --> 01:00:27,824
By the way,

879
01:00:29,959 --> 01:00:33,730
I'll keep this
until you sign the contract.

880
01:00:34,931 --> 01:00:37,500
Or I won't get the money at all.

881
01:00:37,567 --> 01:00:38,668
Do as you please.

882
01:00:39,335 --> 01:00:41,871
You're very clever, aren't you?

883
01:00:42,405 --> 01:00:45,642
I never fail on these matters.

884
01:00:55,451 --> 01:00:56,552
You're good.

885
01:00:58,521 --> 01:01:00,490
I've got it.

886
01:01:04,861 --> 01:01:05,828
Thanks.

887
01:01:24,480 --> 01:01:28,818
We heard that the surgery
was for a very rare case.

888
01:01:28,885 --> 01:01:30,420
That's true.

889
01:01:30,486 --> 01:01:34,090
This is the third case in the world.

890
01:01:34,524 --> 01:01:39,028
And it is the first achievement
in Japan.

891
01:01:40,997 --> 01:01:44,200
I've always been...

892
01:01:44,634 --> 01:01:48,838
They hired Michiko Daimon
as our official resident.

893
01:01:49,539 --> 01:01:51,307
- What?
- Therefore...

894
01:01:51,607 --> 01:01:52,675
I decided to quit.

895
01:01:53,242 --> 01:01:54,143
Bye.

896
01:01:56,345 --> 01:01:58,548
I've always trained themselves.

897
01:02:00,850 --> 01:02:01,718
Office Manager,

898
01:02:03,152 --> 01:02:05,388
isn't Michiko Daimon here yet?

899
01:02:05,455 --> 01:02:08,124
- She has arrived, but...
- I see.

900
01:02:09,792 --> 01:02:10,793
Sir,

901
01:02:10,860 --> 01:02:14,030
the doctor who succeeded
in this difficult operation

902
01:02:14,097 --> 01:02:16,699
was a freelance surgeon?

903
01:02:16,766 --> 01:02:20,203
No, no, that's not true.

904
01:02:22,105 --> 01:02:28,211
The surgeon in charge was
an official resident in this hospital.

905
01:02:31,547 --> 01:02:33,282
MICHIKO DAIMON

906
01:02:33,349 --> 01:02:35,218
FROM MICHIKO DAIMON:
I WON'T DO THAT

907
01:02:35,284 --> 01:02:36,319
Daimon!

908
01:02:41,557 --> 01:02:45,161
Wait. Wait. Wait.

909
01:02:45,528 --> 01:02:47,063
- Prof. Hiruma.
- Yes?

910
01:02:47,130 --> 01:02:50,566
May we have the name of the surgeon?

911
01:02:50,633 --> 01:02:53,236
Name?

912
01:02:53,636 --> 01:02:55,471
Oh, the name.

913
01:02:56,072 --> 01:02:57,807
Let's see...

914
01:02:57,874 --> 01:02:59,509
It is our surgeon

915
01:02:59,909 --> 01:03:05,715
who belongs to
our department of surgery.

916
01:03:10,186 --> 01:03:12,221
- And his name is Ebina.
- What?

917
01:03:14,223 --> 01:03:15,391
Ebina. Come forward.

918
01:03:16,692 --> 01:03:17,593
Excuse me.

919
01:03:20,596 --> 01:03:23,466
I think you've gone too far.

920
01:03:23,533 --> 01:03:25,935
It's fine when I say so.

921
01:03:26,836 --> 01:03:28,871
Step forward.

922
01:03:30,773 --> 01:03:34,143
I'd like to introduce you to
the surgeon who operated

923
01:03:34,210 --> 01:03:38,014
from our surgery department,
Dr. Ebina.

924
01:03:38,080 --> 01:03:40,917
- What is your first name?
- It's Takashi.

925
01:03:42,018 --> 01:03:43,486
Oh, it's Takashi. Okay.

926
01:03:44,187 --> 01:03:46,455
This is Dr. Takashi Ebina.

927
01:03:47,390 --> 01:03:49,659
You have to look over there.

928
01:03:51,494 --> 01:03:53,996
He will be our new chairperson...

929
01:03:54,497 --> 01:03:56,732
The one who does nothing

930
01:03:56,799 --> 01:04:00,136
survives in an organization.

931
01:04:05,208 --> 01:04:08,311
Hello, Kurumi. You did very well.

932
01:04:08,911 --> 01:04:09,979
Please support her.

933
01:04:10,046 --> 01:04:12,181
Yes. You did very well.

934
01:04:13,783 --> 01:04:17,186
Who is this? I don't know him.

935
01:04:17,687 --> 01:04:20,489
- He's so scary.
- I'm not scary.

936
01:04:20,556 --> 01:04:22,525
- Mom!
- Don't be scared.

937
01:04:23,626 --> 01:04:26,262
In a way, he's got the best luck.

938
01:04:26,329 --> 01:04:27,997
EBINA ELECTED AS CHAIRPERSON

939
01:04:31,467 --> 01:04:35,404
Gosh! I lost all my money!

940
01:04:36,806 --> 01:04:39,809
So, what are you going to do now?

941
01:04:40,443 --> 01:04:43,579
I'll stay in the hospital.
I haven't changed my thoughts.

942
01:04:44,480 --> 01:04:47,650
I will get powerful in the organization.

943
01:04:47,717 --> 01:04:48,684
I see.

944
01:04:49,852 --> 01:04:53,356
I'm going to use the organization,
not be used by the organization.

945
01:04:53,890 --> 01:04:55,024
I see.

946
01:04:56,192 --> 01:04:57,627
It's what you did this time.

947
01:04:58,661 --> 01:05:01,030
I just did an operation
I really like.

948
01:05:08,070 --> 01:05:10,806
Hey, would you like to
bet on a horse?

949
01:05:11,774 --> 01:05:13,042
I won't do that.

950
01:05:13,109 --> 01:05:14,377
Play table tennis?

951
01:05:14,443 --> 01:05:15,511
I won't do that.

952
01:05:16,078 --> 01:05:18,080
- Beef rice bowl?
- No thanks.

953
01:05:19,248 --> 01:05:20,383
Public bath?

954
01:05:21,217 --> 01:05:22,084
No thanks.

955
01:05:30,760 --> 01:05:31,894
He's dead.

956
01:05:41,837 --> 01:05:45,274
I'm asking you to connect me
to Director Hachiya.

957
01:05:45,741 --> 01:05:48,678
I've been calling him
since this morning.

958
01:05:49,345 --> 01:05:52,581
How can a meeting take so long?

959
01:05:54,283 --> 01:05:56,519
Alright then. Okay, I understand.

960
01:05:57,687 --> 01:05:58,788
Damn it!

961
01:06:03,893 --> 01:06:05,294
Hello.

962
01:06:05,361 --> 01:06:08,164
Hello, Prof. Mabuchi.

963
01:06:11,334 --> 01:06:12,268
Hello.

964
01:06:12,335 --> 01:06:15,071
Hello. It's been a while,

965
01:06:15,471 --> 01:06:16,639
Mr. Busujima.

966
01:06:18,474 --> 01:06:21,477
I heard
you couldn't keep Michiko Daimon.

967
01:06:23,412 --> 01:06:25,848
How did you know?

968
01:06:26,983 --> 01:06:29,852
If you had been able to keep her,

969
01:06:29,919 --> 01:06:35,391
you could've saved yourself.

970
01:06:35,825 --> 01:06:36,892
Be saved?

971
01:06:37,960 --> 01:06:38,828
Excuse me,

972
01:06:42,031 --> 01:06:43,966
what's that supposed to mean?

973
01:06:45,334 --> 01:06:47,536
You were bored, dear?

974
01:06:54,844 --> 01:06:56,879
What do you have in mind?

975
01:06:56,946 --> 01:06:57,847
What do I have?

976
01:06:57,913 --> 01:07:01,550
What kind of a plan do
you two have in mind?

977
01:07:02,752 --> 01:07:08,057
I just wanted to save
the girl from Takamatsu. That's all.

978
01:07:11,927 --> 01:07:14,630
You're talking nonsense, sir.

979
01:07:15,031 --> 01:07:16,032
Nonsense?

980
01:07:18,300 --> 01:07:21,237
Didn't you remember anything

981
01:07:21,837 --> 01:07:25,174
after meeting Michiko Daimon?

982
01:07:26,542 --> 01:07:27,610
Remember?

983
01:07:29,879 --> 01:07:31,213
About what, sir?

984
01:07:31,580 --> 01:07:34,483
Didn't you remember
that you were a doctor?

985
01:07:42,892 --> 01:07:45,061
Kazuyo. What was that about?

986
01:07:46,128 --> 01:07:48,264
You called Mr. Busujima, dear.

987
01:07:48,898 --> 01:07:51,567
- Did I say that?
- Yes, you did.

988
01:07:51,634 --> 01:07:55,938
Well, well. Let it go, Hiru-chan.
Forget about the past.

989
01:07:56,005 --> 01:08:00,709
I thought so. I knew about you two.

990
01:08:00,776 --> 01:08:03,646
It's all in the past. Grow up.

991
01:08:04,780 --> 01:08:07,750
By the way,

992
01:08:08,451 --> 01:08:10,920
I got a permanent residency in Paris.

993
01:08:11,487 --> 01:08:14,323
I'll never come back to Japan.

994
01:08:14,924 --> 01:08:15,825
Are you quitting?

995
01:08:15,891 --> 01:08:20,296
The only thing that can hug me is...

996
01:08:22,765 --> 01:08:25,401
the sky of Paris.

997
01:08:26,969 --> 01:08:28,604
That's it.

998
01:08:44,420 --> 01:08:45,387
Au revoir.

999
01:08:46,822 --> 01:08:47,790
Kazuyo...

1000
01:08:53,696 --> 01:08:57,967
Hey. What did she just say?

1001
01:08:59,235 --> 01:09:00,836
- I don't remember.
- Excuse me.

1002
01:09:02,338 --> 01:09:03,372
Here's a tea.

1003
01:09:04,406 --> 01:09:05,908
This just came.

1004
01:09:06,375 --> 01:09:08,544
From Totei Medical Hospital.

1005
01:09:10,346 --> 01:09:12,014
Too bad it came.

1006
01:09:12,448 --> 01:09:14,083
It really did come.

1007
01:09:14,149 --> 01:09:15,151
Yes, it did.

1008
01:09:16,552 --> 01:09:18,754
- I should go.
- Already?

1009
01:09:20,756 --> 01:09:22,625
It really came.

1010
01:09:34,803 --> 01:09:36,472
TO: SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

1011
01:09:36,539 --> 01:09:40,142
UNANIMOUSLY AGREED

1012
01:09:41,577 --> 01:09:43,812
DISMISSED

1013
01:09:47,316 --> 01:09:51,820
Please let me play with you.

1014
01:09:51,887 --> 01:09:54,089
I hear a voice.

1015
01:09:54,156 --> 01:09:56,058
Could it be Michiko?

1016
01:09:56,125 --> 01:09:58,260
- She dumped 100 million away.
- Shut up.

1017
01:09:58,327 --> 01:10:00,329
She threw 100 million away.

1018
01:10:00,396 --> 01:10:04,900
What was she thinking?

1019
01:10:04,967 --> 01:10:06,435
You're still nagging about that?

1020
01:10:06,502 --> 01:10:09,672
I don't think Michiko
who dumped 100 million deposit

1021
01:10:09,738 --> 01:10:13,642
would dare come back here.

1022
01:10:13,709 --> 01:10:15,377
That's enough.

1023
01:10:15,444 --> 01:10:17,513
Ron! Jun-nomi.

1024
01:10:17,580 --> 01:10:19,215
Wow.

1025
01:10:29,124 --> 01:10:31,760
Hello?
This is Kanbara Doctor Agency.

1026
01:10:32,261 --> 01:10:34,196
Michiko Daimon?

1027
01:10:35,531 --> 01:10:38,234
Do you mean Daimon
who dumped 100 million?

1028
01:10:38,300 --> 01:10:39,201
She's here.

1029
01:10:39,735 --> 01:10:41,337
It's a shop called Banharn.

1030
01:10:42,438 --> 01:10:45,140
Not a shop.
He's an intern from Thailand.

1031
01:10:45,207 --> 01:10:46,775
- What does he want?
- What is it?

1032
01:10:48,644 --> 01:10:52,214
Hiromi, someone may buy you
for 30 million yen.

1033
01:10:52,281 --> 01:10:53,749
Am I that cheap?

1034
01:10:53,816 --> 01:10:56,819
I like your outfit.
Give it to me for 3,000 yen.

1035
01:10:56,885 --> 01:10:58,354
- Sold. You can buy it.
- See?

1036
01:10:58,420 --> 01:10:59,521
What?

1037
01:11:01,090 --> 01:11:03,225
Michiko, who dumped 100 million yen.

1038
01:11:03,292 --> 01:11:04,460
Fly to Thailand now.

1039
01:11:05,094 --> 01:11:08,163
His friend is a good friend
of a rich man in Thailand

1040
01:11:08,230 --> 01:11:10,566
and he wants you to treat his son.

1041
01:11:10,633 --> 01:11:13,369
- What's that?
- A son of a rich man.

1042
01:11:13,702 --> 01:11:16,238
You can marry into a rich family.

1043
01:11:16,305 --> 01:11:19,875
You'll finally meet someone.
Might as well get married.

1044
01:11:21,010 --> 01:11:24,179
<i>This is a story</i>
<i>about a maverick female doctor.</i>

1045
01:11:24,246 --> 01:11:25,648
Fly!

1046
01:11:29,018 --> 01:11:31,520
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities.</i>

1047
01:11:31,987 --> 01:11:33,889
<i>Medical care has become a world</i>

1048
01:11:34,189 --> 01:11:37,793
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

1049
01:11:38,327 --> 01:11:42,931
<i>To save this crisis in the world</i>
<i>of medical care, a freelance doctor,</i>

1050
01:11:43,465 --> 01:11:46,835
<i>in another word,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

1051
01:11:48,137 --> 01:11:50,339
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

1052
01:11:51,373 --> 01:11:55,411
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

1053
01:11:55,477 --> 01:11:57,313
Please wait here.

1054
01:11:59,114 --> 01:12:04,119
<i>Her medical certifications and</i>
<i>work experience are her only weapons.</i>

1055
01:12:06,622 --> 01:12:11,327
Maybe the son of a millionaire could
just be a giant elephant.

1056
01:12:15,931 --> 01:12:17,199
Thanks for waiting.

1057
01:12:21,437 --> 01:12:23,639
Are you Dr. Daimon?

1058
01:12:24,073 --> 01:12:25,574
Yes, I am.

1059
01:12:26,141 --> 01:12:30,446
Can you operate on my dearest son?

1060
01:12:31,280 --> 01:12:33,315
Of course. You can depend on me.

1061
01:12:33,382 --> 01:12:35,851
This is my dearest son.

1062
01:12:37,119 --> 01:12:38,053
Where is he?

1063
01:12:44,193 --> 01:12:45,227
So tiny.

1064
01:12:45,627 --> 01:12:47,763
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

1065
01:12:48,530 --> 01:12:49,531
Can you do it?

1066
01:12:51,400 --> 01:12:52,067
Yes.

1067
01:12:52,735 --> 01:12:53,869
I never fail.

1068
01:12:54,503 --> 01:12:57,339
<i>She is known as Doctor-X.</i>
